# Redirect rules that ship with the site (Netlify reads this file from dist/_redirects).
# Host normalisation, legacy /zeroed/* pages, dashboard and API rules live in netlify.toml.
#
# RETIRED PAGES -> 410 Gone, served with the custom 404 page as the body (src/pages/404.astro).
# 410 tells Google the removal is deliberate, so it drops the URL faster than a 404; sending unrelated
# pages to the homepage would be treated as a soft 404. Rules without ! never override a real file, so
# re-publishing one of these slugs later just works. To retire a page, append its path here.
#
# POLICY (SEO_STRATEGY.md section 2, rule 1; enforced by scripts/verify-protected.mjs at the end of `npm run build`):
#   - Never delete, 410, 404, noindex or redirect a page listed in seo/protected-urls.txt (every URL with at least one
#     Search Console impression in 16 months), unless it is in seo/approved-removals.txt with a dated, founder-written line.
#   - A retired URL with zero impressions may be retired with 410, or 301-ed to a page that answers the SAME query.
#     Never 301 to an unrelated page or to the homepage (Google reads that as a soft 404).
#   - Before adding any 410 or 301 line, check the path against seo/protected-urls.txt. The build fails if a protected
#     path has a 301/302/404/410 rule or no built page.
#   - Log every change to this file in seo/CHANGES.md.

